# Try the API without curl/Postman: install the "REST Client" extension, then click "Send Request"
# above any request below. Start the API first (F5, or Terminal -> Run Task -> Run API).
# Run them top to bottom the first time. (Interactive docs are also at http://localhost:8000/docs)

@host = http://localhost:8000/api/v1

### 1. Register (change the email if it already exists)
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "owner@myshop.in",
  "password": "a-long-passphrase",
  "full_name": "Shop Owner"
}

### 2. Log in
# @name login
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "owner@myshop.in",
  "password": "a-long-passphrase"
}

### 3. Who am I
GET {{host}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 4. Create a company (also creates roles, financial year and invoice numbering)
# @name company
POST {{host}}/companies
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "My Shop",
  "gstin": "27ABCDE1234F1Z5",
  "financial_year_start_month": 4
}

### 5. My companies
GET {{host}}/companies
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 6. Current company + my permissions (company-scoped calls need X-Company-Id)
GET {{host}}/companies/current
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}
X-Company-Id: {{company.response.body.$.id}}

### 7. Roles
GET {{host}}/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}
X-Company-Id: {{company.response.body.$.id}}

### 8. Audit trail
GET {{host}}/audit-events
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}
X-Company-Id: {{company.response.body.$.id}}

### 9. Refresh the access token (paste your refresh_token from step 2's response)
POST {{host}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "PASTE_REFRESH_TOKEN_HERE"
}
